! The `ph.x` input that generated `reference.out.ph-alas-epsilon-us-soc`, so that
! the reference is regenerable rather than merely committed.
!
!   pw.x -in alas-epsilon-us-soc.in && ph.x -in alas-epsilon-us-soc.ph.in
!
! with `outdir` pointing at the same scratch for both. The dielectric constant
! and the Born charges are what `epsil = .true.` prints at the end.
! (fully-relativistic ultrasoft AlAs, a polar crystal with spin-orbit coupling.)
dielectric constant of AlAs, ultrasoft, spin-orbit
 &inputph
  tr2_ph = 1.0d-14,
  epsil = .true.,
  fildyn = 'alas-soc.dynG',
  amass(1) = 26.98,
  amass(2) = 74.92,
 /
0.0 0.0 0.0
